# wgl_contract_probe64.expected - output of wgl_contract_probe.c (x86_64 build) run on winoracle.
# Oracle: Windows 11 10.0.26200, Microsoft "GDI Generic" OpenGL 1.1.0 (see gl-vendor / gl-renderer / gl-version).
# The i686 build gives identical output except env pointer-size (diff wgl_contract_probe32.expected).
# Line shape: <tag> ret=<value> gle=<GetLastError, "untouched" = the call left the seeded sentinel alone> [detail].
# gle values: 6 ERROR_INVALID_HANDLE, 87 ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER, 127 ERROR_PROC_NOT_FOUND, 170 ERROR_BUSY,
# 2000 ERROR_INVALID_PIXEL_FORMAT. A positive ret with a stray gle (e.g. swap-buffers gle=6) is a leftover,
# not an error: only a failing ret makes gle meaningful.
# 
# ================================================================================
# ChoosePixelFormat selection rule (measured; pf-list shows the 36 formats it chooses among)
# ================================================================================
# Reproduced by tools/oracle_probe/wgl_choosepf_model_check.py: the rule below picks the identical index
# for all 152 machine-readable (reqraw=) requests in the choose-* lines.
# 
# Candidates are all pf-list indices 1..36 (36 = pf-list count). Memory DCs see the same list
# (choose-mem-dc-baseline, choose-mem-dc-bmp). The returned index is the candidate with the smallest
# key below, compared in order; ties go to the LOWEST index. It never fails on a valid DC (ret >= 1 for
# every case); there is no "no match" result.
#   1. Number of {PFD_DRAW_TO_BITMAP, PFD_SUPPORT_GDI} requested but absent from the format.
#      (choose-draw-to-bitmap-db ret=1, choose-support-gdi ret=1, choose-prio-bmp-db-color24 ret=13,
#       choose-prio-gdi-db-color16 ret=19: a bitmap/GDI request beats a double-buffer request.)
#   2. Double-buffer mismatch: (request has PFD_DOUBLEBUFFER) != (format has it). Skipped entirely when
#      PFD_DOUBLEBUFFER_DONTCARE is set. Asking for NO double buffer prefers single-buffered formats.
#      (choose-baseline ret=3, choose-single-buffer ret=1, choose-doublebuffer-dontcare ret=1,
#       choose-doublebuffer-dontcare-with-db ret=1, choose-prio-db-dontcare-depth16 ret=2,
#       choose-prio-db-vs-color24 ret=3, choose-prio-db-color16 ret=3.)
#   3. PFD_DRAW_TO_WINDOW requested but absent from the format.
#      (choose-prio-window-vs-color16 ret=1, choose-prio-window-vs-color24 ret=1,
#       choose-prio-window-vs-accum32 ret=2, choose-prio-colorindex-window-color16 ret=9,
#       choose-prio-win-bmp-color24 ret=1.)
#   4. Sum of four 0/1 mismatches, all equal weight:
#        colour:  format.cColorBits != requested, where a requested cColorBits that is not one of
#                 4, 8, 16, 24, 32 (including 0, 48) counts as 32
#                 (choose-sweep-color-bmp: 0,1,3,5,9,12,15,17,20,25,31,33,40 all -> a 32-bit format;
#                  4, 8, 16, 24 -> the exact-depth BMP formats 32, 26, 20, 14; choose-color-0 ret=3).
#        accum:   only if requested cAccumBits != 0: format.cAccumBits != requested (EXACT equality;
#                 33, 65, 128 match nothing; 0 means "don't care", it does not prefer accum-0 formats)
#                 (choose-sweep-accum-db, choose-sweep-accum-bmp16, choose-prio-color16-vs-accum64 ret=2,
#                  choose-prio-color24-vs-accum32 ret=14).
#        pixtype: format.iPixelType != requested
#                 (choose-colorindex-8 ret=11, choose-prio-colorindex-bmp-color8 ret=29).
#        alpha:   only if requested cAlphaBits != 0: mismatch when the format has 0 alpha bits; any
#                 requested value 1..16 behaves like "want alpha" (choose-sweep-alpha-db: 1, 8, 16 -> 7;
#                 choose-alpha-8 ret=7).
#      Because the four terms are summed and ties go to the lowest index, a pixel-type request loses to an
#      alpha or accum request that only an RGBA format can meet (choose-prio-colorindex-vs-alpha8 ret=7,
#      choose-prio-colorindex-vs-accum64 ret=3), and colour 16 loses to accum 64
#      (choose-prio-color16-vs-accum64 ret=2) but wins against accum 32 or 33 or 65.
#   5. Depth: formats whose cDepthBits >= requested come first, smallest depth first; if none reaches the
#      request, the largest depth. PFD_DEPTH_DONTCARE makes the requested depth 0.
#      (choose-sweep-depth-db: 0..16 -> depth 16 (ret=4), 17..64 -> depth 32 (ret=3);
#       choose-depth-more ret=3; choose-depth-dontcare / -24 / -64 ret=4;
#       choose-prio-single-depth-dontcare ret=2.)
#   6. Lowest index.
# Request fields with NO observable effect (every candidate ties on them): cStencilBits
# (choose-sweep-stencil-db, all stencil 8), cAuxBuffers (choose-aux-1), iLayerType (choose-layer-overlay,
# choose-layer-underlay), PFD_STEREO / PFD_STEREO_DONTCARE (choose-stereo, choose-stereo-dontcare),
# PFD_GENERIC_FORMAT / PFD_GENERIC_ACCELERATED / PFD_SWAP_* / PFD_NEED_PALETTE / PFD_SUPPORT_DIRECTDRAW /
# composition bit 0x8000 (choose-generic-*, choose-swap-*, choose-need-palette, choose-support-directdraw,
# choose-support-composition), per-channel accum/colour bit fields (choose-accum-64-per-channel), nSize and
# nVersion (choose-nsize-0 / -10 / -39 / -100, choose-nversion-0 / -2, choose-all-zero ret=2,
# choose-zero-but-nsize ret=2: no validation). PFD_SUPPORT_OPENGL is carried by every format.
# Argument errors: ppfd == NULL faults (choose-null-ppfd EXC=0xc0000005, ret 0); hdc == NULL returns 0 with
# gle=6 (choose-null-hdc). Round trip: choose-exact requests each pf-list entry verbatim and gets the same
# index back for all 36.
# The rule is a fit that reproduces every probed request; combinations that the 36 formats cannot
# distinguish (e.g. stencil, aux, layer) are not claimed.
# 
# ================================================================================
# Other contracts measured in this file
# ================================================================================
# pf-list / describe-*: 36 formats. 1,2,5,6,9,10 = WIN|BMP|GDI|GL|GENERIC|COMPOSITION (0x807c), single buffer,
#  32-bit; 3,4,7,8,11,12 = DB|WIN|GL|GENERIC|SWAPCOPY|COMPOSITION (0x8465), the only double-buffered formats;
#  13..36 = BMP|GDI|GL|GENERIC (0x78) only, 24/16/8/4-bit colour. describe-index0 / describe-index-count+1:
#  ret 0 gle 87; describe-nbytes-39: ret 0 gle 87 and the struct is untouched; describe-nbytes-0 and
#  describe-null-ppfd return the count (36) without writing; describe-null-hdc: ret 0 gle 6.
# setpf-*: SetPixelFormat succeeds once per DC (setpf-A-db); a second call fails even for the same index
#  (setpf-second-same ret 0 gle 2000) and GetPixelFormat keeps the first; index 0, count+1, negative:
#  ret 0 gle 87; ppfd NULL is accepted (setpf-null-ppfd ret 1); NULL hdc: gle 6. getpf-unset ret 0.
# create-*: no pixel format on the DC -> NULL gle 2000 (create-no-pixel-format, create-memdc-no-format);
#  NULL hdc -> NULL gle 6 (create-null-hdc); a memory DC holding the default 1x1 monochrome bitmap cannot
#  take a pixel format (create-memdc-default-bitmap-setpf ret 0 gle 1); a memory DC with a 32-bit DIB
#  takes format 1 and renders (create-memdc-dib, make-memdc-dib, memdc-render readback 255,0,0,255);
#  a window-format context cannot be made current on that bitmap DC (make-window-format-ctx-onto-bitmap-dc
#  ret 0 gle 2000).
# make-*: wglMakeCurrent(NULL,NULL) with NOTHING current returns 0 with gle 6 (make-null-null-nothing-current);
#  with a context current it returns 1 and releases it (make-null-null-releases). (hdc, NULL) releases and
#  returns 1 (make-dc-null-ctx-releases, also with nothing current: make-dc-null-ctx-nothing-current ret 1).
#  (NULL, ctx) returns 0 gle 6 and leaves the current context alone (make-null-dc-ctx-while-current).
#  A DC with no pixel format: ret 0 gle 2000 (make-dc-without-pixel-format). Mismatched pixel format
#  (double-buffered context onto a single-buffered DC, or the reverse): ret 0 gle 2000
#  (make-mismatched-format, make-mismatched-format-rev), and when another context was current the failed call
#  RELEASES it (make-mismatched-while-current-after cur-ctx=NULL). A different window with the SAME format
#  is accepted (make-same-format-other-window ret 1). Making the already-current pair current again returns 1.
#  Second thread: the same context cannot be made current while current on another thread
#  (make-second-thread-same-ctx-same-dc, ...-other-dc: ret 0 gle 170 ERROR_BUSY), a different context can
#  (make-second-thread-other-ctx ret 1), and the same context can be taken once released
#  (make-second-thread-after-release ret 1). Deleted or garbage HGLRC: ret 0 gle 6 (make-deleted-hglrc,
#  make-garbage-hglrc). A thread with nothing current calling (NULL,NULL) gets ret 0 gle 6
#  (make-second-thread-null-null-nothing-current).
# delete-*: wglDeleteContext on the calling thread's current context returns 1 and leaves the thread with no
#  current context (delete-current: cur-ctx-after=NULL); delete of another thread's current context: ret 0 gle
#  170 (delete-second-thread-current-ctx); twice / NULL / garbage: ret 0 gle 6.
# share-*: wglShareLists(a,b) succeeds on fresh contexts (share-before) and then both see each other's lists
#  and textures (share-before-visibility); it also succeeds when only the first argument already owns
#  objects, which become visible in the second (share-after-gentextures, share-after-gentextures-visibility);
#  it FAILS with ret 0 gle 87 when the second (destination) context already generated objects
#  (share-after-gentextures-dst, share-after-gentextures-both), when already shared (share-already-shared),
#  and with itself (share-self); NULL arguments / deleted context: gle 6. Different pixel formats may share
#  (share-different-format ret 1). Objects survive deletion of the context that created them
#  (share-source-deleted-visibility). wglShareLists(c,c) on a context that is current on ANOTHER thread:
#  ret 0 gle 170 ERROR_BUSY (share-second-thread-current-ctx; the same self-share on the owning thread is gle 87).
# gpa-*: with NO current context every name, including "" and NULL, returns NULL with gle 6 and never faults
#  (gpa-noctx). With a context current only genuinely extension names the implementation exports return
#  non-NULL (glColorTableEXT, glAddSwapHintRectWIN); core 1.1 names (glVertex3f, glGenTextures), unknown
#  names and "" return NULL with gle 127; a NULL name faults (gpa-ctx name=(NULL) EXC=0xc0000005).
# swap-*: SwapBuffers works on a double-buffered DC with no context current (swap-buffers-no-ctx-double ret 1)
#  and on a memory DC (swap-buffers-memdc ret 1); single-buffered DC: ret 0 (swap-buffers-no-ctx-single,
#  swap-buffers-single-while-other-current); no format / NULL: ret 0 gle 6. wglSwapLayerBuffers(MAIN_PLANE)
#  and (OVERLAY1), (UNDERLAY1) and 0 all return 1 on the double-buffered DC (swap-layer-*), 0 with gle 2000
#  on a DC with no format or NULL, 0 on the single-buffered DC.
# viewport-*: the first make-current of a context sets viewport and scissor to the whole client area
#  (viewport-initial 0,0,320,200); resizing the window to 400x300 does NOT change them, nor does making
#  current again, release-and-make, or SwapBuffers after another resize (viewport-after-resize-*); an
#  explicit glViewport survives (viewport-explicit-then-resize-remake); a NEW context first made current
#  after a resize gets the new size (viewport-second-context-first-make 0,0,500,400).
# noctx-*: with no current context (fresh thread, after release, or on a thread other than the one that holds a
#  context) nothing faults: glGetError returns 1282 (GL_INVALID_OPERATION) on every call (it is not
#  cleared), glGetString returns NULL, glIsEnabled / glIsTexture / glGenLists return 0, and glGetIntegerv /
#  glGetFloatv / glGetBooleanv / glGenTextures leave the output untouched (untouched=1); GL calls are no-ops.
#  wglGetCurrentContext / wglGetCurrentDC return NULL.
#
# opengl32's own pixel-format / layer / default-proc exports (tags wglpf-*, wgllayer-*, wgldefproc-*):
#  wglChoosePixelFormat, wglDescribePixelFormat, wglGetPixelFormat and wglSetPixelFormat give the same
#  return, last error and output as the gdi32 call on the same input in the same order (every wglpf-X line
#  equals its wglpf-X-gdi line), and a format set through one is seen by the other (wglpf-cross-*).
#  No pixel format has a layer plane: wglDescribeLayerPlane(plane 1) and wglSet/GetLayerPaletteEntries,
#  wglRealizeLayerPalette(plane 1) fail with ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER 87 and write nothing; plane 0 fails
#  with the last error untouched; on the palette calls a NULL hdc or a DC without a format is 2000
#  (describe: 6 for a NULL hdc, 87 without a format). wglGetDefaultProcAddress: NULL / 127 for core and
#  unknown names, with or without a context (it returns non-NULL for two extension names, which Vitreo
#  does not expose).
# swapmulti-*: DWORD wglSwapMultipleBuffers(UINT n, const WGLSWAP*) returns a bit mask, bit i set when entry i
#  succeeded (swapmulti-two-main 0x3, bad-then-good 0x2, good-then-bad 0x1, max16 0xffff). n = 0 is 0 with the
#  last error untouched (zero-null, zero-nonnull); n > 16 (WGL_SWAPMULTIPLE_MAX) is 0 with gle 1
#  ERROR_INVALID_FUNCTION and nothing is swapped (over-max17, over-max20); n = 1 with a NULL array faults
#  (null-array EXC=0xc0000005). Per entry, as wglSwapLayerBuffers: a double-buffered DC succeeds for any
#  uiFlags (overlay1, flags0, all-bits; only a MAIN_PLANE entry leaves the stray gle 6 SwapBuffers leaves),
#  with or without a current context (one-main-noctx); a single-buffered DC or a DC without a format fails
#  with the last error untouched (single, no-format); a NULL hdc fails with 6 (null-hdc). The same DC twice
#  succeeds twice (same-dc-twice 0x3).
env pointer-size=8
env windows=10.0.26200
env window-client=320x200 visible=0
pf-list count=36
